From: Brian Rauchfuss - PCD <brauchfu@pcocd2.intel.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Apr 94 14:50:11 PDT
Subject: [#94-4-152] Life Extension

> I was wondering if any of you have any experience with the following.
> 1) Diet restriction on yourself or another.

I could send you the FAQ on calorie restriction (it is probably too big to send
to the entire list).  I don't use it, but the research results are impressive
(large increases in the life span of rats, and good preliminary results from 
monkey tests).  Unfortunately it is not easy to do, since you need to maintain
a high nutrient intake while slowly decreasing calories.

> 3) The free radical stuff(I am very sceptical of this myself)

The free radical theory of aging is a pretty strong contender to "The Truth"; 
the results showing disease reduction due to anti-oxidants are strong enough
to justify taking them on that basis alone.

> What sort of strategies would you suggest, and how do you justify those
> strategies.

I presently use: low-fat diet for disease reduction and anti-oxidants for both
disease reduction and possible life-extension.

> In general, what has been going on in the field of aging research, I
> haven't been on top of all of the literature for about 5-6 years.(just a
> tick of the clock:-)

There is a drug which is reported to increase the limited number of times
cells can divide, which has important implications for life-extension.

